{"team":"CAR","col":"#3AC7F0","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":58.5,"adot":7.5,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>A Ground-First Machine</h2><p>The tight end is barely used in the passing game (8% of targets vs ~15%) \u2014 fade their TE's receiving props.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>They run downhill \u2014 mostly inside the tackles (21% to the edge vs ~25%), a gap/power scheme that trades big plays for a steady, grinding floor.</p><p>This is a deliberate, low-volume offense \u2014 just <strong>58 plays a game</strong> (league ~61), which quietly caps the ceiling on everybody's targets and carries.</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>pass-first</strong> (55% pass), which puts scoring equity on <strong>Tetairoa McMillan</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 Soft on the Ground</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR1s</strong> \u2014 73 rec yds/game (vs ~58). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They surrender <strong>152 rushing</strong> and <strong>229 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR2s \u2014 just 28 rec yds/game (vs ~36); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They leak <strong>RB rushing TDs</strong> (0.63/game vs ~0.46) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.54/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>Broadly a leaky unit \u2014 48% success rate allowed (vs ~44%); points come easy against them.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>Chuba Hubbard</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts; <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Bryce Young","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":25,"props":{"C